# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `dist` is rebuilt by Vercel on every deploy, so it is never committed.
dist/
build/

# ── Stale build/verification artifacts ────────────────────────────────────
# These were produced by earlier local build checks. They are byte-for-byte
# copies of `public/` plus old hashed bundles, so they carry no source that
# is not already in the tree — untracked so a fresh clone stays small.
.buildcheck-*/
.vb-verify-*/
.verify-build*/
dist-verify*/

# Build snapshots taken under a throwaway name while checking a UI change
# (`dist-h`, `dist-r2`, `dist-shots`, …). Rebuilt on demand and never
# committed — `dist/` above is the one Vercel actually produces.
frontend/dist-*/

# A manual archive of the tree and a zero-byte file a stray shell redirect
# left behind. Neither is source; both were sitting untracked in the root.
sch-path.zip
=

# ── Environment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only the *example* templates are committed; real values are set in the
# Vercel / Render dashboards and never enter the repository.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Legacy JSON fallback store. Nothing in backend/src reads it — the system is
# MySQL-only — and it holds a plaintext `centerhead` credential, so it must not
# be committed. Left on disk rather than deleted; see the note in the handoff.
backend/data/store.json

# ── Local analysis scratch files ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Bundle-composition reporters and static smoke servers used while profiling
# and verifying the build. They are throwaway tooling, not part of the app.
.bundle-analyze.cjs
.smoke-serve.cjs
*.local-analyze.*

# ── Agent working data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The WorkBuddy agent's own folder: memory notes, plans, prompts and scratch
# files, plus the recon/audit probes (Playwright sweeps, RBAC snapshots, DB
# integrity scripts) that carry hardcoded seeded credentials and the Railway
# host. None of it is application source — a clone does not need it and some of
# it must not ship. Left on disk; only untracked.
.workbuddy-ai/

# ── Editor / OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Scratch renders produced while checking generated PDFs.
*-render.png
